## Credible Sources Used

The following authoritative resources were consulted to verify information about psychotherapy, preparing for an initial appointment, therapist qualifications, confidentiality, and treatment expectations.

1. **National Institute of Mental Health (NIMH)** — [Psychotherapies](https://www.nimh.nih.gov/health/topics/psychotherapies)\
   Provides guidance on selecting a therapist, understanding professional qualifications, evaluating treatment approaches, discussing therapy goals, and asking about confidentiality.
1. **American Psychological Association (APA)** — [Understanding Psychotherapy and How It Works](https://www.apa.org/topics/psychotherapy/understanding)\
   Explains what to expect during an initial psychotherapy appointment, how to prepare, what information to bring, and how to evaluate a potential therapist.
1. **American Psychological Association (APA)** — [How to Choose a Psychologist](https://www.apa.org/helpcenter/choose-therapist)\
   Provides guidance on professional credentials, clinical experience, therapeutic compatibility, treatment methods, and financial considerations.
1. **Association for Behavioral and Cognitive Therapies (ABCT)** — [Guidelines for Choosing a Therapist](https://www.abct.org/fact-sheets/guidelines-for-choosing-a-therapist/)\
   Offers practical information about therapist qualifications, treatment approaches, session fees, scheduling, and questions to ask before beginning therapy.
1. **Texas Behavioral Health Executive Council (BHEC)** — [License Verification](https://bhec.texas.gov/tbhec/verify-a-license/)\
   Provides an official resource for verifying applicable behavioral health professional licenses in Texas.
1. **National Institute of Mental Health (NIMH)** — [Help for Mental Illnesses](https://www.nimh.nih.gov/health/find-help)\
   Provides guidance on finding appropriate mental health care, evaluating providers, and understanding treatment options.

*These sources provide general educational information. Individual treatment recommendations, professional licensing requirements, and confidentiality obligations depend on the provider, applicable laws, and individual circumstances.*

